## Why This Is Asked

Regulated, large-scale NLP systems require auditable provenance, per-tenant governance, and secure artifact management. This question probes how to architect for verifiable model provenance, drift detection, and safe rollouts across tenants and languages.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant enclaves and policy evaluation
- Cryptographic signing and KMS/HSM
- Immutable audit trail with Merkle proofs
- Data lineage and privacy controls
- Drift detection across tenants
- Safe rollout and rollback (canary/blue-green)
- Governance and auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: sign artifact with KMS and record hash in ledger
function signArtifact(artifact, kmsClient, ledger) {
  const hash = hashArtifact(artifact);
  const signature = kmsClient.sign(hash);
  ledger.append({ hash, signature, timestamp: Date.now() });
  return signature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale provenance checks as tenants scale to thousands?
- How would you verify rollback integrity without downtime in a live channel?

